    "intro_html":  "Pad kee mao means drunken noodles, and depending on who you ask it is named for what you eat after a night out or what you want to drink while eating it. Either way it is wide rice noodles seared in a hot pan with chile, garlic, basil and a dark salty sauce, and it is the noodle dish nobody else on this site is making. Each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e587 calories and 26 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.25\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). There is a reason it lands where it does, and I am going to name it.",
